# UIS numbers

The handbook is the live page `https://www.uiscom.ru/academiya/spravochnyj-centr/dokumentatsiya-api/data_api/`. Read it again before any UIS change. It can change. Do not invent methods, paths, or fields. Do not commit a copy of that page.

The host is the literal `https://dataapi.uiscom.ru/v2.0`. Do not use `dataapi.comagic.ru`. HTTPS only. Do not follow redirects. Do not trust a custom certificate. Timeout 30s. Body cap 20 MB. `Content-Type` is `application/json; charset=UTF-8`. One JSON-RPC object. No batch. `jsonrpc` is `2.0`. POST is the transport. It is not a mutation.

This release may send only:

- `get.virtual_numbers` for purchased numbers. The stored field is `virtual_phone_number`. Do not sort this method: `virtual_phone_number` is not sortable.
- `get.available_virtual_numbers` for free numbers. The stored fields are `phone_number`, `onetime_payment`, and `monthly_charge`. Sort a free read page and the free access page by `phone_number` ascending. Count probes and the access like-probe send no sort.

Never send `user_id`. The key is a permanent client `access_token`. Do not call `login.user`, `logout.user`, `enable.virtual_numbers`, `disable.virtual_numbers`, `get.customer_users`, `get.available_ct_phone_prefixes`, or any other method. The method name is a literal in the envelope builder. Do not accept a method, a field, a filter, or a sort from a caller, a flag, or a saved catalog.

`limit` is at most 10000. `offset` is at most 100000 and a multiple of 10000. One unfiltered window is 110000 numbers. That is a per-request cap. A longer list is split by prefix until every leaf fits. String `>` is not used. Filters are only the ones the walk builds: omitted for a leaf of at most 110000, `like` with one trailing `%`, `=` of a prefix when that prefix is split further, and regexp `^[^0-9]` or `^` plus the prefix plus `[^0-9]`. Child totals must sum to the parent. A sum mismatch, a filter the field rejects, a non-digit remainder that is still too big, or a prefix longer than 15 digits that is still too big does not publish. After a list, the unfiltered total is counted again. If it moved, nothing is published. Purchased leaves are offset-only. Free leaves are sorted.

The access check reads one purchased page of `limit` 1000, one purchased `like` probe `0%` with `limit` 1, then the same pair for free numbers. The first failure stops. A probe with total 0 is access. A short page is not access. A full first page of a longer list is access. Every number on the access page must be admitted. The check claims the lease and does not write catalogs or the stage log.

A number is the digit string the tariff split already accepts. Do not convert 8 to 7. A formatted number fails the page. The same number twice on one page or on a later page of the same list fails that list. There is no `ON CONFLICT`. An empty complete list replaces the UIS slice of that catalog. The same number in both drafts stays purchased. All `get.virtual_numbers` statuses are purchased. Do not store redirection, category, location, status, name, comment, or campaigns. A free price that is null, invalid, negative, or scientific notation leaves that cell empty and the page still succeeds. Purchased money columns stay empty. City, region, ABC, and the local number come from the tariff split.

A JSON-RPC `error` fails the call even on HTTP 200. The response `id` must match the request `id`. Transport, timeout, empty body, non-JSON, a body over 20 MB, and HTTP 5xx retry once. HTTP 4xx and JSON-RPC errors do not use that retry. `limit_exceeded` with `limit_type` `minute` and `minute_reset` from 0 to 90 waits once and repeats that call once. A day limit fails the walk. A successful page with `minute_remaining` 0 waits once when the reset is 0 to 90, then returns that page. `day_remaining` 0 fails the page. The operator error may show a mnemonic matching `^[a-z0-9_]+$` and at most 200 characters of `message`. Drop the message when it contains the key, `://`, `bearer`, `password`, `token`, `key=`, or `access_token`. Never copy `error.data.value`, `extended_helper`, or `params`.

Each call costs one point. A failed purchased list does not open the free list. Both lists must succeed before either catalog is replaced. The provider literal is `UIS`. Publish locks only `uis_sync_state`, deletes and inserts free numbers, then purchased numbers. Tariff resplit locks SipOut, then Runexis, then UIS. The key stays ciphertext. Do not log the key, the body, or the URL. An API key cannot call these routes. The stage log is `data/numbering-sync/uis.txt`.
